# 📖 Books of Worlds — Interactive Puzzle Game

**Books of Worlds** is an interactive fantasy puzzle game 🎮 where players explore different worlds, solve environmental puzzles 🧩, and guide unique creatures through challenging levels.

## ✨ Features

* 🌍 Multiple worlds and chapters
* 🧩 Interactive puzzle mechanics
* 🐉 Creature-based challenges
* 🌦️ Seasonal and environmental mechanics
* 🎯 Objectives, hints, and move tracking
* 🏆 Level completion statistics
* 🎬 Animations and visual effects
* 🔐 User registration and login
* 🛡️ JWT authentication

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

HTML5 | CSS3 | JavaScript | Three.js | Node.js | Express.js | JWT | bcrypt

## 🎯 Project Objective

The project combines **game development, interactive UI design, puzzle-solving, backend APIs, authentication, and JavaScript development** into an interactive web application.

🚀 A project focused on creativity, problem-solving, and full-stack web development.

🎮 How to Play — Books of Worlds
📖 Start the Game
Open the game and enter the Book of Worlds.
🌍 Choose a World
Select an available world and choose a chapter/level.
🧩 Understand the Objective
Each level gives you objectives. Read the riddle, hint, and objective panel before making moves.
🐾 Guide the Creatures
Move each creature through the environment and guide it to its home/destination.
🌦️ Use the Environment
Change seasons or activate available mechanics such as Rain, Wind, Lily Pads, Moonbeam, Torch, Tide, Vines, and Portal Stones to create the correct path.
📚 Fold & Reveal Paths
Some levels contain different terrain layers. Fold/reveal the layers to discover paths needed by different creatures.
🎯 Complete All Objectives
Finish the required objectives and guide all creatures home.
🏆 Earn Stars
Complete the chapter efficiently. Your moves and time are recorded on the completion screen.
🔄 Retry or Continue
After completing a level, you can continue to the next level, retry the current level, or return to the chapter map.

💡 Tip: Different creatures have different requirements. For example, the Rabbit needs underground tunnels, Fish need water, Birds need updrafts/open sky, and Bears can break stone doors
